<!-- 4. SLOT ALGORITHM -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-num">4</div>
    <div class="section-title">Slot Availability Algorithm</div>
  </div>
  <div class="section-subtitle">Runs every time a customer requests available slots. All 7 steps must pass for a slot to appear. If any step fails, the slot is excluded.</div>

  <div class="algo-grid">
    <div class="algo-card">
      <div class="algo-step-num">Step 1</div>
      <div class="algo-step-title">Check store is open</div>
      <div class="algo-step-body">
        Fetch business_hours for the day_of_week. Check business_hours_exceptions for holidays on that exact date.<br><br>
        → Store closed: return empty list<br>
        → Holiday (is_closed = true): return empty list<br>
        → Exception with custom hours: use those instead
      </div>
      <span class="algo-db">business_hours · business_hours_exceptions</span>
    </div>

    <div class="algo-card">
      <div class="algo-step-num">Step 2</div>
      <div class="algo-step-title">Apply same-day minimum notice</div>
      <div class="algo-step-body">
        If the requested date is today: earliest slot = NOW() + same_day_notice_hours.<br><br>
        Default: 4 hours. Configurable per store.<br><br>
        Prevents booking a 2-hour makeup session that starts in 30 minutes.
      </div>
      <span class="algo-db">stores.same_day_notice_hours</span>
    </div>

    <div class="algo-card">
      <div class="algo-step-num">Step 3</div>
      <div class="algo-step-title">Build blocked ranges from existing bookings</div>
      <div class="algo-step-body">
        Fetch all bookings for this artist on this date with a blocking status:<br><br>
        <strong>held · pending · approved · deposit_paid · confirmed</strong><br><br>
        Each booking = blocked time range. New slot cannot overlap any of these.
      </div>
      <span class="algo-db">bookings WHERE status IN blocking_statuses</span>
    </div>

    <div class="algo-card">
      <div class="algo-step-num">Step 4</div>
      <div class="algo-step-title">Apply travel buffer for cross-store bookings</div>
      <div class="algo-step-body">
        Fetch artist bookings at OTHER stores on this date.<br><br>
        Weekday (Mon–Thu): block 150 minutes before + after<br>
        Weekend (Fri–Sun): block 90 minutes before + after<br><br>
        Example: Tripoli ends 9:10am on a weekday → no Beirut slots before 11:40am.
      </div>
      <span class="algo-db">artist_store_buffers · bookings (other stores)</span>
    </div>

    <div class="algo-card">
      <div class="algo-step-num">Step 5</div>
      <div class="algo-step-title">Apply processing gap support</div>
      <div class="algo-step-body">
        For services with active_duration_min (kreatin, hair color):<br><br>
        • CHAIR blocked for full service duration<br>
        • ARTIST only blocked for active_duration_min<br>
        • Artist can take another client during processing gap
      </div>
      <span class="algo-db">services.active_duration_min</span>
    </div>

    <div class="algo-card">
      <div class="algo-step-num">Step 6</div>
      <div class="algo-step-title">Flag early bird slots</div>
      <div class="algo-step-body">
        If the store has early_bird_cutoff set:<br><br>
        • Slots before cutoff → is_early_bird = true<br>
        • Early bird slots carry an additional early_bird_fee<br>
        • Still offered — just priced differently<br><br>
        Beirut default: before 9:00 AM. Tripoli: before 7:30 AM.
      </div>
      <span class="algo-db">stores.early_bird_cutoff · stores.early_bird_fee</span>
    </div>

    <div class="algo-card special" style="grid-column:span 2">
      <div class="algo-step-num">Step 7 — Final</div>
      <div class="algo-step-title">Generate valid slots</div>
      <div class="algo-step-body" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px">
        <div>
          Iterate through the store open window in service_duration_min increments. For each candidate slot [start, end):
          <div class="algo-check">start ≥ earliest_allowed_time (after minimum notice)</div>
          <div class="algo-check">end ≤ store closing time</div>
          <div class="algo-check">[start, end) does not overlap any blocked range</div>
          <div class="algo-check">start + service_duration ≤ closing time</div>
          <br>
          If all pass → add to available list. Tag as early_bird if applicable.
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="algo-gist">
            <div class="algo-gist-title">🔒 GIST constraint — the final atomic guard</div>
            <div class="algo-gist-body">Even after all 7 steps pass, the GIST exclusion constraint on the bookings table is the last line of defence.<br><br>If two customers race for the same slot at exactly the same moment, only one INSERT succeeds. The second receives SLOT_UNAVAILABLE instantly. No application-level check can provide this guarantee — only the database constraint can.</div>
          </div>
          <span class="algo-db" style="margin-top:10px">Output: TimeSlot[] with start_time, end_time, is_early_bird, early_bird_fee</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

