| **`B-Edge-Multi-Artist-Salon-Plan-v1.md`** | **New, Sep 21, 2026.** Six phases, 34 tasks, with the sequencing argued rather than assumed: **unify `subscriptionVisibleCond` before regraining subscriptions** (three copies, already drifted once); **capture the slot baseline before touching the scheduler**, because after migration 047 it can no longer be taken; **authorisation before membership**, or the first invited artist can immediately edit the owner's prices. Phases 1–2 are the business request and ship independently; 3–5 change money and can follow. Ends with the single acceptance test the whole design serves — *an artist working alone must not be able to tell that multi-artist support exists* — and a table mapping each HLD risk to the specific task that carries it. |

