## Development Reference

| Script | What it is for |
|---|---|
| `scripts/capture-slot-baseline.py` | **New, Sep 21, 2026.** Captures every bookable (artist, store, service) triple's slot output across a 90-day horizon into `project-docs/slot-baseline-pre-046.json`, then `--compare`s a later run against it. Exists because migration 047 makes slot generation intersect store hours with a per-artist rota, and the only honest proof that an artist with no rota is unaffected is byte-identical output captured beforehand. Paced at 1.2/s under the 600-per-5-min rate limiter — an earlier version fired at 8-way concurrency and 2,191 of 2,790 samples came back 429, which a harness that treated a failed call as an empty list would have recorded as a calendar with no availability. Exits non-zero if any sample errors, and reports how many triples actually produced availability so a mostly-empty baseline cannot pass as a strong gate. |
| `scripts/verify-uc7.py` | **New, Sep 21, 2026.** `make verify-uc7`. Proves the salon owner/member boundary against a running stack. Borrows one real salon: moves `salons.owner_id` to a stand-in, logs the **same account** back in as a member, attempts every owner-only write, and restores ownership in a `finally`. One account and one set of routes, with the role as the only variable — comparing two different accounts would confound the role with whatever else differs between them. Checks effects, not just status codes: after a refused write it re-reads the row and requires it byte-identical. |



